{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's switch it on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's see what it does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3660,
    "dDurationMs": 5109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through this coil of thick wire, we're about\nto pass a huge alternating electric current."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8769,
    "dDurationMs": 2721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top is a 1 kg aluminium plate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11490,
    "dDurationMs": 2769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we hear that noise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14259,
    "dDurationMs": 2321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's that noise?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16580,
    "dDurationMs": 12520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the vibration of the plate, because it's\nvibrating at two times the frequency of this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Woah!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Woooaaaahhhhhhh!!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hahaha, how does it do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's magical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find out, I've come to the place where\nit all started - The Royal Institution in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "London"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36100,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the key to Faraday's magnetic lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38120,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's amazing that the lock still works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40860,
    "dDurationMs": 5859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From the 1870's on this became a store room,\nwhich is why it survived and it survived intact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46719,
    "dDurationMs": 4381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the joinery giant electromagnet are exactly\nthe same as Faraday left it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51100,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is exactly as Faraday would have had\nit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53130,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right, yup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54130,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Faraday's time it was known that electric\ncurrent creates a magnetic field, but it remained"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58690,
    "dDurationMs": 4869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an open question whether the reverse is possible\n-- if a magnetic field could generate electric"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63559,
    "dDurationMs": 1371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "current."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64930,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Faraday answered this question with his most\nfamous apparatus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68160,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Faraday's electromagnetic induction ring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71970,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74760,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In August, 1831 Faraday wrapped two coils\nof insulated wire around this iron ring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80330,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 1831 you could not go down to your\nlocal electrical hardware shop and ask for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84070,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "x hundred meters of insulated wire, you had\nto insulate the wire as you went."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87230,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as you pushed and pulled the wire in and\nout of the ring you had to insulate it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90320,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It takes 10 working days, which was a huge\ninvestment of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93180,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the investment paid off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95070,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Faraday connected a battery to one of\nthe coils, he saw a brief pulse of current"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99560,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the other coil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100580,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when he disconnected the battery, he saw\na pulse of current in the other direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105000,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He realized that current was induced in the\nsecond coil only when the magnetic field through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109490,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110490,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if they hadn't been wrapped on the same\nring, Faraday may have noticed that the two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114520,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coils repel each other when the current is\ninduced and that's due to the interaction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118790,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their magnetic fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120500,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which brings us back to this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122450,
    "dDurationMs": 5290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through the bottom coil we are passing a huge\nelectric current: 800A which alternates in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127740,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "direction 900 times per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130640,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This ensures there will always be a changing\nmagnetic field above the coil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134890,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of a second coil we're using the Aluminium\nplate, but the principle is the same, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139480,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changing magnetic field induces currents in\nthe plate that create an opposing magnetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144230,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "field -- so it levitates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147140,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How awesome is that?!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151660,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This current is not only good for levitating\nthe plate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154170,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can also make lightbulbs glow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157950,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A gift."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158950,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uh, thank you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160110,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161110,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162110,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not too close because it will burn the lamps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165250,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I put it there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167530,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168530,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just as current in a toaster element heats\nit up, the induced current in the plate dissipates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172720,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its energy as heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173740,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And some water too\nThank you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175230,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah to see the temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176900,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Check out how hot this plate is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180960,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, that is nuts!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183270,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is this your favorite demo?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186170,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a flying BBQ or something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189650,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tell me this is not the best dinner table\ncenterpiece."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192450,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It levitates, gives you light, and you can\ncook on it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195650,
    "dDurationMs": 29860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all the while you're demonstrating Faraday's\nLaw of electromagnetic induction."
    } ]
  } ]
}
